body:
Hello,
Apple allows reading the picked file only after the user picked it, after that you will get this error.
Currently as a workaround to allow reading bytes from `KmpFile` in iOS, I'm copying the picked file to a new temp file created by the library and I'm using that new file for any read operations which is not controlled by Apple and will remain available for a longer time.

What do you need to do with the file exactly? is `KmpFile.readByteArray` not enough for you? Otherwise I can think of changing the temp file that I talked about as public API.

```kotlin
actual class KmpFile @InternalCalfApi constructor(
    val url: NSURL, // This is the url returned by Apple and you need to directly read it after picking the file otherwise it won't be available
    internal val tempUrl: NSURL, // This is the copy url created by Calf and used in  `readByteArray` and remain available
) {
    @OptIn(InternalCalfApi::class)
    constructor(url: NSURL) : this(url, url)
}
```

@MohamedRejeb I was expecting that the `android.permission.POST_NOTIFICATIONS` permission will already be set when using the `com.mohamedrejeb.calf:calf-permissions-notifications` module. Why isn't it specified in the manifest? That would be one less set up step:

<img width="797" height="572" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/edbbfb15-154b-49a5-ad37-e4d0d7bbd036" />

Also this permission is *not* always granted on Android.
